       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 20 mg once daily is twice the labeled maximum dose of amlodipine for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a typical starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n3. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I'll do this if you confirm the dose is intentional. A note with the rationale, such as \"dose exceeds the usual maximum, confirmed by attending,\" would help pharmacy and nursing.\n4. **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is the usual next step.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
